WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:22.078
Rat and Mole ate in Badger's warm kitchen.

2
00:00:22.079 --> 00:00:26.400
No one spoke until the plates were empty.

3
00:00:26.401 --> 00:00:30.216
"We're sorry that we bothered you," said Rat.

4
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:34.150
"I'm glad to help," said Badger.

5
00:00:34.151 --> 00:00:36.914
Badger gave them some tea.

6
00:00:36.915 --> 00:00:39.857
"Now tell me," said Badger.

7
00:00:39.858 --> 00:00:42.600
"How is Toad?"

8
00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:45.476
Rat was surprised.

9
00:00:45.477 --> 00:00:50.473
Normally Badger did not talk about Riverbankers.

10
00:00:50.474 --> 00:00:55.545
"How's Toad?" said Rat. "Not good."

11
00:00:55.546 --> 00:00:59.454
"He crashed another car last week," said Mole.

12
00:00:59.455 --> 00:01:02.879
"He's a very bad driver," said Rat.

13
00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.700
"But he thinks he's the best in the world."

14
00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:10.473
"How many has he had?" asked Badger.

15
00:01:10.474 --> 00:01:15.279
"Do you mean crashes or cars?" asked Mole.

16
00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.945
"It's the same thing," laughed Rat.

17
00:01:20.946 --> 00:01:27.014
"Seven! His yard is full of broken cars."

18
00:01:27.015 --> 00:01:31.608
"He went to the hospital three times," said Mole.

19
00:01:31.609 --> 00:01:35.620
"Soon he'll run out of money!" said Rat.

20
00:01:35.621 --> 00:01:38.280
"Or he'll get killed!"

21
00:01:38.281 --> 00:01:42.078
"Shouldn't we do something?" said Mole.

22
00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:45.208
Badger rubbed his chin.

23
00:01:45.209 --> 00:01:48.401
"The other animals will have to help.

24
00:01:48.402 --> 00:01:52.280
But we must wait until spring," he said.

25
00:01:52.281 --> 00:01:58.614
"In winter all the animals are too sleepy."

26
00:01:58.615 --> 00:02:01.164
Rat and Mole nodded.

27
00:02:01.165 --> 00:02:05.437
"I'm sleepy," said Rat.

28
00:02:05.438 --> 00:02:07.783
"It's time for bed."

29
00:02:07.784 --> 00:02:11.900
"I'm sleepy too," yawned Mole.

30
00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:15.738
"Come along," said Badger.

31
00:02:15.739 --> 00:02:20.471
Badger led them to their beds.

32
00:02:20.472 --> 00:02:22.347
Badger was right.

33
00:02:22.348 --> 00:02:29.901
In winter animals can't do anything too active.
